PCA:

1. Principle Component Analysis
2. No target so it is comes under unsupervised algorithm.
3. This can also be used in the preprocessing.
4. PCA converts the any number of column into a specific column

Note:
a. When we have column which is similar and you can't choose any column because all the column
looks same and fine. Then you should choose PCA.
b. PCA wont be selecting the column, instead it creates a new column
c. no of new column that we needed will be decided on n_components parameter